<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BRL comfortable with 1997 forecast.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BRL comfortable with 1997 forecast.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian wine producer BRL Hardy Ltd said on Thursday that it was comfortable with analysts' forecasts of a profit of about A$23.5 million before abnormal items for the 1997 calendar year.</p>
<p>&quot;All we can say is at this stage we are very comfortable with that forecast. We will be targeting higher,&quot; BRL Hardy managing director Stephen Millar told a news conference.</p>
<p>For 1996, the company reported a profit of A$21.2 million after tax and before abnormals.  </p>
<p>Millar said the company was targeting double digit sales growth up to the turn of the century after exceeding the A$300 million level in 1996 for the first time.</p>
